    "user_request_original": "Design a 21-layer alternating Ge/ZnS dielectric bandpass filter on CaF2 substrate for normal incidence. Layer sequence: Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge (21 finite layers). Initialize all layer thicknesses using quarter-wave optical thickness estimates at 4.45 μm center wavelength with ±20% uniform random jitter, bounded to 50-500 nm per layer. Optimize using L-BFGS-B algorithm with Hessian approximation enabled. Evaluate transmittance at four wavelength bands: maximize in 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm, minimize in 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Design and thickness-optimize a 21-layer alternating Ge/ZnS dielectric bandpass filter on a CaF2 substrate for normal incidence. Initialize layers to 400 nm within 50–500 nm bounds. Maximize transmittance in 4.15–4.35 μm and 4.55–4.75 μm, minimize transmittance in 3.60–4.00 μm and 4.85–5.20 μm using L-BFGS-B optimization.",
